<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῠσᾰρ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύσος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>foul, dirty</i>: hence,
				<i>loathsome, abominable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἷμα μητρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1624
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Le.</u>
				18.23
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυσερός</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; μ. μηδέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.37
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			, -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ώταται πράξεις</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Sto.</u>
				339.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>defiled, polluted</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1393
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				1350
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				340
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				2.20
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρῶς</span>
			
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυστικῶς</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Zos.
				4.3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
